{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Come near to me, please, and they came near.</b> Midrash: because he said above, 'Cause every man to go out from me,' and the Egyptians were standing outside and inclining their ears to hear what they were saying — therefore when he said, 'I am Joseph your brother, is my father still alive?' he was not concerned if they hear. But when he wanted to say, 'whom you sold me,' he did not want them to hear, because he intended to settle his brothers in Egypt, and had they heard that they sold their brother, they would say: they are very wicked men, who even sold their own brother — all the more so will they do evil to us if they dwell among us. Therefore he said to them, 'Come near to me, please,' and I will tell you in secret. Another interpretation: at first he said to them, 'I am Joseph your brother, is my father still alive?' and he did not want to mention his sale, on account of Benjamin his brother — so they would not be ashamed before him and so he would not tell his father. He moved them to the side and said to them, 'Come near to me, please'; he separated them from Benjamin and said, 'I am Joseph your brother, whom you sold me.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:07.557146998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}